@inherits LocalizedComponent

@*
    The playground's counterpart to the site's BrandHeading.astro: the mark, the product name
    as this app's one <h1>, and the tagline — same copy, same tokens, so the two halves of the
    product read as one. Simplified from the site's version in one place: no script measures
    the mark against the heading's own cap height here, it is sized to look right at the sizes
    this app actually renders — a fixed-image alignment where the original does a measured one.
*@

<div class="brand-heading">
    <h1>
        <img class="mark" src="/favicon-64.png" srcset="/favicon-64.png 2x, /favicon-128.png 4x" alt="" width="64" height="64" decoding="async" />JustDummies
    </h1>
    <p class="tagline">@PlaygroundStrings.T(LocaleState.Current, "brand.tagline")</p>
</div>
